From: EternalMikaelson <klaus_mikaelson@rediffmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:04:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] camera: Strip OppoGallery dependence in thumbnail-tap launch

GalleryHelper opens the gallery from the camera thumbnail through an
explicit-package launch guarded by resolveActivity(), with an OEM
error dialog as the fallback. On AOSP the resolution fails, so the
thumbnail cannot open the gallery and no other gallery app can be
used.

Replace the thumbnail-click method (the one that reports
"thumbnail_click") with a plain ACTION_VIEW intent: MIME type video/*
when the video flag is set, image/* otherwise, the item Uri as data,
FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION, then startActivity(). Android's
default-app resolution then picks the gallery.

